{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"c":0.5,"y":0.046511627815394085,"t":"1718867188","h":0.008720930389296444,"x":0.7716049391467531,"w":0.069958845774332645},{"h":0.014856366583259173,"w":0.098859246571858725,"y":0.097222979482590843,"x":0.1007761379304551,"c":1,"t":"PART 4"},{"w":0.65843617757161454,"c":1,"x":0.1028806799384724,"t":"Scientists believe that a majority of the earth's bird population migrate in some fashion or","h":0.011627906062437354,"y":0.12354651189126198},{"x":0.1028806683842574,"c":1,"y":0.13808139522898044,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"other. Some travel seasonally for relatively short distances, such as birds that move from","w":0.65637858072916666},{"h":0.013250883392226243,"y":0.15253239099320215,"c":1,"w":0.65432098388671878,"t":"their winter habitats in lowlands to mountain tops for the summers. Others, like the Arctic","x":0.10288066024218362},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"t":"Tern, travel more than 25,000 miles seasonally between the northern and southern poles.","y":0.16715116268415831,"x":0.10288065015606709,"w":0.66460906982421875},{"h":0.011629619081674591,"c":1,"w":0.64609054565429691,"y":0.1816843345092255,"t":"Bird migration has been studied over many centuries through a variety of observations.","x":0.10288065299033572},{"x":0.10288065833365181,"c":1,"w":0.66666666666666674,"y":0.20347467625751703,"t":"But until relatively recently, where birds went to in the winter was considered something of","h":0.011778563015312105},{"w":0.65432098388671867,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.10288066347502185,"c":1,"y":0.21643109567161367,"t":"a mystery. The lack of modern science and technology led to many theories that we now"},{"w":0.67489710489908861,"y":0.23110465104179445,"c":1,"t":"recognize as error-filled and even somewhat amusing. Take hibernation theory for example","x":0.10082305241725237,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"c":1,"t":"- two thousand years ago, it was commonly believed that when birds left an area, they went","x":0.10082303417798509,"w":0.68312759399414058,"h":0.011778563015312105,"y":0.24705535919213695},{"y":0.26148409919924021,"x":0.10288066553710072,"t":"underwater to hibernate in the seas and oceans. Another theory for the regular appearance","w":0.6748971048990885,"h":0.010318226471666136,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"and disappearance of birds was that they spent winter hidden in mud till the weather changed","x":0.10284236161716867,"y":0.27435273270335425,"w":0.69143595377604172,"h":0.013496617967585389},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"x":0.10288066206970393,"y":0.28916372177514837,"w":0.64197530110677081,"c":1,"t":"and food became abundant again. The theory that some birds hibernate persisted until"},{"t":"experiments were done on caged birds in the 1940s which demonstrated that birds have no","c":1,"w":0.6769547526041666,"y":0.30377906966090973,"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.10288064828422799},{"y":0.31831395337939927,"w":0.14609053293863933,"c":1,"x":0.10288065940339214,"h":0.010307954534344299,"t":"hibernation instinct."},{"x":0.10076105568051484,"h":0.015512431046988073,"w":0.64414606730143231,"c":1,"y":0.33852832367752606,"t":"One of the earliest naturalists and philosophers from ancient Greece was Aristotle who"},{"w":0.67695475260416671,"t":"was the first writer to discuss the disappearance and reappearance of some bird species at","x":0.10288064829134025,"c":1,"y":0.35453474702026222,"h":0.011778563015312216},{"y":0.36918604640524799,"w":0.68106994628906259,"x":0.10288066461100015,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"t":"certain times of year. He developed the theory of transmutation, the seasonal change of one"},{"y":0.3822143695936393,"h":0.013250883392226243,"t":"species into another, by observing redstarts and robins. He observed that in the autumn,","w":0.66255142211914064,"c":1,"x":0.10082305424013943},{"c":1,"x":0.10077865711712557,"t":"small birds called 'redstarts' began to lose their feathers, which convinced Aristotle that they","y":0.39545173791509725,"h":0.015912291298766368,"w":0.6811707560221355},{"t":"changed into robins for the winter, and back into redstarts in the summer. These assumptions","x":0.10283392459432823,"y":0.41095186171147646,"w":0.68939539591471355,"h":0.01413838012479629,"c":1},{"h":0.015511825031329862,"t":"are understandable given that this pair of species are similar in shape, but are a classic","x":0.10280545469543806,"y":0.42406564764576005,"c":1,"w":0.64623148600260416},{"c":1,"x":0.10288065646055509,"w":0.51234568277994785,"y":0.44040697663672757,"t":"example of an incorrect interpretation based on correct observations.","h":0.011627907185728592},{"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"The most bizarre theory was put forward by an English amateur scientist, Charles Morton,","y":0.46220930221921974,"w":0.66666666666666663,"x":0.1028806583290328,"c":1},{"t":"in the seventeenth century. He wrote a surprisingly well-regarded paper claiming that birds","y":0.47673733778149674,"w":0.67283950805664061,"x":0.098765431053025737,"h":0.01308824372937456,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.10288066021108259,"y":0.49116607778875032,"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.65432098388671878,"t":"migrate to the moon and back every year. He came to this conclusion as the only logical"},{"h":0.013088698100706786,"c":1,"x":0.10281793924573152,"t":"explanation for the total disappearance of some species.","y":0.5043827869494415,"w":0.4219462585449219},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.81893004153995586,"c":1,"t":"Q31","y":0.26017441846595923,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q32","y":0.38226744170203208,"c":1,"x":0.81893004154638593,"w":0.034979422887166378},{"t":"Q33","w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.81893004153995586,"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.42587209288456385,"c":1},{"w":0.034979422887166267,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"Q34","c":1,"x":0.81893004161197236,"y":0.47529069749145791},{"w":0.67901234944661459,"y":0.54651162780040063,"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.10288065643146353,"c":1,"t":"One of the key moments in the development of migration theory came in 1822 when a white"},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"x":0.1028806665139346,"c":1,"t":"stork was shot in Germany. This particular stork made history because of the long spear in","y":0.56095406352372579,"w":0.66872426350911462},{"x":0.10082304702720572,"y":0.57558139524212582,"w":0.65432098388671878,"c":1,"h":0.011627907185728703,"t":"its neck which incredibly had not killed it - everyone immediately realised this spear was"},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.66049382527669276,"c":1,"y":0.59010600702596216,"t":"definitely not European. It turned out to be a spear from a tribe in Central Africa. This was","x":0.10288065926572093},{"c":1,"x":0.10082303686585542,"w":0.66460906982421886,"t":"a truly defining moment in the history of ornithology because it was the first evidence that","h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.60306242663860488},{"w":0.65226338704427089,"x":0.10288065218941179,"y":0.61773255803007343,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"storks spend their winters in sub-Saharan Africa. You can still see the 'arrow stork' in the","c":1},{"t":"Zoological Collection of the University of Rostock in Germany.","x":0.10288066113709893,"w":0.46090535481770833,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.63221436994233216,"c":1},{"y":0.65400471134476723,"w":0.66460906982421875,"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"People gradually became aware that European birds moved south in autumn and north in","c":1,"x":0.10288065016856725},{"h":0.014552004064912638,"y":0.66860465102804612,"w":0.66872426350911451,"t":"summer but didn't know much about it until the practice of catching birds and putting rings","x":0.098765440229753379,"c":1},{"y":0.68153178924107105,"x":0.10077455708624247,"t":"on their legs became established. Before this, very little information was available about the","w":0.68530390421549481,"h":0.0161675176856374,"c":1},{"w":0.68930043538411456,"h":0.011778563015312216,"t":"actual destinations of particular species and how they travelled there. People speculated that","c":1,"y":0.69758539485427151,"x":0.10288064641058364},{"t":"larger birds provided a kind of taxi service for smaller birds by carrying them on their backs.","c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.10288064833259503,"y":0.71220930220499945,"w":0.67695475260416671},{"t":"This idea came about because it seemed impossible that small birds weighing only a few","y":0.72673733778141802,"x":0.10082303699782026,"h":0.01308824372937456,"c":1,"w":0.66460906982421875},{"w":0.69135803222656256,"y":0.73837209324136999,"c":1,"t":"grams could fly over vast oceans. This idea was supported by observations of bird behaviour","x":0.10082304340317962,"h":0.016044867754824943},{"c":1,"w":0.41358024597167975,"x":0.10288065880714138,"t":"such as the harassment of larger birds by smaller birds.","y":0.75581395338064983,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"t":"Q35","x":0.81893004153995586,"y":0.56104651148921503,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"w":0.034979422887166378},{"w":0.034979422887166267,"x":0.81893004161197236,"y":0.60319767423564385,"c":1,"t":"Q36","h":0.013081395583944722},{"x":0.81893004202777708,"y":0.68023255792318371,"c":1,"h":0.015988372380376759,"w":0.039094648361205908,"t":"Q37"},{"c":1,"t":"Q38","x":0.81893004181753659,"y":0.72529069749145791,"h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.037037035624186254},{"x":0.84773662590209575,"y":0.86773255797837645,"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"111"},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30618598937988273,"y":0.95318838622914936,"h":0.03366544698798335,"c":1,"x":0.66992475471958191}]}